{"id":"H6424","lemma":"פָּלַס","transliteration":"palas","sayIt":"PA-las","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to envy","meaning":"1) (Piel) to weigh, make level, balance\n1a) to weigh out\n1b) to make level or smooth","glosses":["mete out","cleared","make a level","consider","lord examines","clear"],"count":6,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"psa-58","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"you mete out","kjv":"ye weigh"}},{"chapterId":"psa-78","v":50,"renderings":{"bsb":"He cleared","kjv":"He made"}},{"chapterId":"pro-4","v":26,"renderings":{"bsb":"Make a level","kjv":"Ponder"}},{"chapterId":"pro-5","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"consider","kjv":"Lest thou shouldest ponder"}},{"chapterId":"pro-5","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"and the LORD examines","kjv":"and he pondereth"}},{"chapterId":"isa-26","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"You clear","kjv":"dost weigh"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Psalm 58:2","note":"No, in your heart you plot injustice. You measure out the violence of your hands in the earth.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Proverbs 4:26","note":"Make the path of your feet level. Let all of your ways be established.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Isaiah 26:7","note":"The way of the just is uprightness. You who are upright make the path of the righteous level.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}